customer_joy: Hey team — customer on Hosted API reporting tool/function-calling failures. Root symptoms: our API returns 400 schema validation errors. Model function_call.args sometimes arrives as a JSON string instead of an object, and enum fields (e.g., priority) are coming back lowercase (\"high\") while the customer's schema expects uppercase (\"HIGH\"|\"MED\"|\"LOW\"). They also reported intermittent latency spikes when these calls happen. Can someone triage?

maria: Sorry about that — can you paste the raw request+response and confirm deployment type (Hosted/Dedicated/Private) and SDK version?

customer_joy: Hosted. Using openai-python compat shim v1.8. Minimal repro below. Getting a 400 from our validation layer.

customer_joy: ```json
{
  \"model\": \"gpt-4o-mini\",
  \"messages\": [{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Schedule a meeting\"}],
  \"function_call\": \"auto\",
  \"functions\": [{\"name\":\"schedule_meeting\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"time\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"priority\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"HIGH\",\"MED\",\"LOW\"]}},\"required\":[\"time\",\"priority\"]}}]
}
```

customer_joy: model response we saw:```json
{
  \"id\":\"resp-abc123\",
  \"function_call\": {
    \"name\":\"schedule_meeting\",
    \"arguments\": \"{\\\"time\\\":\\\"2026-03-15T10:00:00Z\\\",\\\"priority\\\":\\\"high\\\"}\"
  }
}
```

dan: This looks like two separate but related compatibility issues: 1) the model sometimes emits the arguments as a string (stringified JSON) instead of a native object, and 2) enum normalization (capitalization/aliasing). Both break strict schema validation. Any idea if a recent runtime change touched streaming or chunk assembly?

customer_joy: We started seeing it after the runtime patch last week, yes.

alex: I can repro locally with a streaming run. When the function_call JSON is split across chunks the assembly path occasionally leaves the inner arguments as a raw string. Also some models emit enum variants (lowercase) depending on sampling. Quick workaround we use in other compat paths: detect string args and JSON.parse them, then map enums case-insensitively to allowed values. Example snippet (Node):

alex: ```js
function normalizeFunctionCall(fc) {
  // fc.arguments may be a string or an object
  let args = fc.arguments;
  if (typeof args === 'string') {
    try {
      args = JSON.parse(args);
    } catch (e) {
      // fallback: keep as string and surface error to caller
      throw new Error('function_call.arguments not valid JSON');
    }
  }
  // normalize enum aliases
  if (args && typeof args.priority === 'string') {
    const map = { 'high': 'HIGH', 'med': 'MED', 'low': 'LOW' };
    const p = args.priority.toLowerCase();
    if (map[p]) args.priority = map[p];
  }
  return { ...fc, arguments: args };
}
```

maria: Can we enable that normalization for this org as a short-term fix? Customer is blocked in prod.

alex: Yes — we can flip the compat-normalizer opt-in for org_1234. I'll also open an internal fix to ensure the streaming assembler emits native objects and to add case-insensitive enum acceptance in the validation layer rather than relying on downstream guests. Opening INF-4923. ETA: initial hotfix (opt-in toggle) within 1 hour, platform patch 24h.

dan: For the latency spike: the extra parsing step is cheap (~100–150ms) but we see spikes up to ~2.8s. I suspect unrelated fallback behavior (quant kernel fallback to CPU path) triggered by the same model variant during that rolling update. Eng-infra should correlate model variant, kernel fallback, and these timestamps.

customer_joy: Appreciate it. Can you also confirm there's no billing/auth break? Customer originally complained billing doubled during retries.

maria: I checked — no 401/403 for their org, but there were retry loops from the client due to 400 responses which increased billed tokens. Recommend enabling normalization so we stop generating client retries.

alex: I've enabled the compat-normalizer opt-in for org_1234 and pushed a feature flag. Please ask customer to retry and share the new model response if any problems. I'll follow up on INF-4923 with a postmortem and a change to accept enum aliases at the validation layer.

support-bot: Created INC-2026 (customer report) and INF-4923 (engineer fix). Assigned to eng-runtime + eng-infra. :white_check_mark:

maria: Thanks all — customer notified and will try repro. If they still see issues, we'll collect request_id and raw logs (request/response) and escalate.

customer_joy: Confirmed after toggle — calls now succeed and no schema errors. Latency back to baseline. Thanks! :rocket:
